<%= content_for :title, t('.title') %>
<%= content_for :meta_tags do %>
  <meta name="description" content="<%= t(".meta_description") %>" />
<% end %>


<div class="background-full-color flex-container text-center">
	<div class="background-title flex-item">
		<h2>BECOME AMBASSADORS FIATOPE</h2>
	</div>
</div>

<div class="info-large text-center">
	You have most certainly made it to the point of being a project proponent that the success of your fundraising campaign, certainly a major step, does not alone ensure the realization of your project. At Fiatope, we are fully aware of the challenge of achieving your ambition. For this, we accompany you beyond fundraising. To this end, we have the honor to count on recognized experts and personalities in the various areas of participatory financing that we cover. These are the Fiatope Ambassadors. They will provide you with valuable support in the search for the right skills to carry out your project. Thanks to their address books and their networks, they can help you in many other ways.
</div>
<div class="container org">
	<div class="info-large">
		<h2>The principle of ambassadors</h2>
		<p>They are an essential part of the Fiatope ecosystem. They help promote the values and goals of the platform. They are the best representatives of Fiatope's ethics and will help you as a project bearer to get the best possible outcome for your commendable initiative. They will also provide inspiration and examples for you, from their experience and the successes they have achieved in their respective fields.</p>
		<h2>Detailed missions of the Ambassador</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>The Ambassador shares and promotes Fiatope ideals, values and goals.</li>
			<li>ILs help you find useful contacts for the realization of your projects and talk about them in their networks.</li>
			<li>They are experts or recognized personalities in their respective fields</li>
			<li>They also invite original project promoters to join the platform</li>
			<li>They participate in the selection of projects in their field.</li>
			<li>They can give you advice on presenting your projects</li>
		</ul>
		<h3>Remuneration</h3>
		<p>Ambassadors are not remunerated for their advice and support</p>
		<h3>Updates from project sponsors</h3>
		<p>The Ambassadors will regularly receive updates from project sponsors on the progress of their funding campaign.</p>
		<h3>Exemptions</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>The role of Ambassadors is not to help you find funds for your project</li>
			<li>Ambassadors can not guarantee the success of your campaign</li>
			<li>Ambassadors can not be held responsible for any difficulties you may encounter during the execution of your campaign.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</div>
